What are Organic Photovoltaics (OPV)?
Organic Photovoltaics (OPV) represent a revolutionary third-generation solar technology utilizing organic semiconductors – carbon-based molecules or polymers – to convert sunlight into electricity. Unlike traditional silicon panels, OPVs offer unique advantages including ultra-thin, lightweight construction, mechanical flexibility, and semi-transparency. These properties enable applications impossible for conventional photovoltaics, from building-integrated solar windows to wearable energy harvesters.
